  "details": "I love the Dolly system and the potential it has for filmmaking in VRC - I think another helpful tool would be to add \"marks\".\n\nIn acting \"hitting your mark\" means to move to the exact spot in the scene where you need to stand to be lit and shot properly. What I'd like to propose is a means to leave marks that all players in the instance can see but do not show up on camera.\n\nThe decal system wouldn't be sufficient imo because you don't want marks to actually show up on the recording (and you only get one at a time), they'd need to be on an ignored layer or something. I'd also caution against a decal at all since you don't know for sure the mark is going to be on solid ground, instead I'd rather see a plain \"x\" or something similar, maybe with an arrow indicating direction?\n\nYou could also perhaps colour-code them, creating marks for multiple actors in one scene.",
